{{Quote|The last time I saw you, you gave me a knife and a loaded blaster and told me to wait in a bunker 'till daylight.|[[Jyn Erso]], to [[Saw Gerrera]]|<ref name="Rogue One: A Star Wars Story">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>}}
[[File:The_hand_with_the_knife.png|thumb|right|200px|[[Arvel Skeen]] holding a knife]]
The '''knife''' was a handheld [[melee weapon]] used for slashing and stabbing. A knife could also be used as a cutting tool or utensil. '''Combat knives''' and '''throwing knives''' were common types of knife. '''[[Vibroknife|Vibro-knives]]''' featured a small, [[Vibroblade|vibrating blade]] that hummed when activated.<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> It was capable of cutting through metal materials, including [[droid]]s and [[stuncuffs]].

A '''Galley knife''' referred to knives used in a [[starship]]'s galley.<ref name="BTC">''[[Battlefront: Twilight Company]]''</ref> In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Date">The section of ''[[Battlefront: Twilight Company]]'' where [[Corbo]] carries a galley knife is set twenty-two [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Clone Wars]], which [[Mission to Mustafar|ended]] in [[19 BBY]], according to ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''. The section must have therefore been based in [[3 ABY]].</ref> the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] recruit [[Corbo]] carried a galley knife when attempting to visit the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] defector [[Everi Chalis]] regarding his pet [[felinx]] which had [[Death|died]] under her orders.<ref name="BTC" />

After the [[First Order]] [[Attack on Tuanul|attack]] on [[Tuanul]], [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] used a knife to free [[BB-8]] from [[Teedo]]'s net.<ref name="TFA novel">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens (novelization)|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' novelization]]</ref>

{{Weapon-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Moving on, we've got Obi-Wan's knife and this is an actual sharp knife.''"<br />"''Is there a reason we would use something that is an actual sharp knife for a prop versus just something that's a dull blade? Does it pick up differently on camera?''"<br />"''Actually it's because if you notice from the scene he was actually cutting a real piece of meat.|A member of the [[Lucasfilm Archives]] and [[Kristin Baver]] discussing the knife prop used in ''Obi-Wan Kenobi''|<ref name="Props">{{ThisWeek|5dYCIFU5q6Y|Obi-Wan Kenobi Props, LEGO Star Wars Summer Vacation, and More!|sw_url=video/obi-wan-kenobi-props-lego-star-wars-summer-vacation-and-more}}</ref>}}
Knives were first identified in the [[Star Wars: The Force Awakens (novelization)|novelization]] of the [[2015]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]<ref name="TFA novel" /> and the [[Star Wars: The Force Awakens (audiobook)|audiobook]] version,<ref name="Audiobook">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens (audiobook)|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' audiobook]]</ref> which were both released on [[December 15]], 2015.<ref name="Novelization release">{{PenguinRandomHouse|url=books/530125/the-force-awakens-star-wars-by-alan-dean-foster/9781101965504|text=The Force Awakens (Star Wars)}} {{C|eBook}}</ref><ref name="Audiobook release">{{PenguinRandomHouse|url=books/530125/the-force-awakens-star-wars-by-alan-dean-foster/9780399567506|text=The Force Awakens (Star Wars)}} {{C|Audiobook download, Random House Audio}}</ref>

During production of the ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' television series, an actual sharp knife was used in the series because [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] cut a real piece of [[Foodstuff|meat]] in the [[Part I|first episode]].<ref name="Props" />

